"""
STEP 14 - Final deliverable: ALL-HAZARD events per storm x ZCTA, daily exposure,
          data dictionary
================================================================================
Builds the files requested by the health team for Louisiana 2018.

  hazard_events_zcta_LA_2018.csv   MAIN TABLE - one row per storm/event x ZCTA for
                                   ANY hazard: stream flooding, stream flooding imputed
                                   from the parish, heavy rain, coastal flooding,
                                   tropical cyclone within 100 km
  flood_events_zcta_LA_2018.csv    streamflow-only version (subset of the above logic)
  zcta_daily_exposure_LA_2018.csv  every ZCTA x every day of 2018 (explicit zeros)
  zcta_universe_LA_2018.csv        every Louisiana ZCTA and which measures it has
  data_dictionary_LA_2018.csv      variables, descriptions, units, types, missingness
  CONVENTIONS.md                   unit, boundary year, zero/absent/missing rules

Hazard days (per ZCTA and local day)
  streamflow      flood day from the ZCTA's own NWM reaches (step 9)
  flood_imputed   ZCTAs without usable reaches take their MAIN PARISH's flood day
                  (step 7); magnitude_source = "imputed (parish)"
  heavy_rain      AORC daily rain or wettest cell-hour with return period >= 2 yr (step 12)
  coastal         nearest tide gauge (<= 40 km) at or above NOAA minor flood level (step 13)
  tc              tropical cyclone closest approach within 100 km, from 1 day before to
                  1 day after (step 13)

Events and storm IDs
  * Streamflow storm-ZCTA rows keep their storm_id from step 10.
  * Hazard days NOT already inside a streamflow storm-ZCTA window form runs per ZCTA
    (<= 1 dry day apart). Runs are grouped when their dates overlap (+/- 1 day) and
    their ZCTAs are <= MERGE_KM apart (or share the same tropical cyclone). A group
    that overlaps a streamflow storm in time and space joins that storm; otherwise it
    becomes a new hazard-only storm (IDs LA2018_H###).
  * Key = (storm_id, zcta), unique; several runs of one ZCTA in one storm are combined.
  * Measures (rain, coastal, cyclone) are computed for the window
    [start_date - 1 day, end_date]; streamflow magnitude, return period and extent only
    exist where streams flooded (or were imputed from the parish).
  * severity_composite (OPTIONAL): mean percentile rank (0-1) of the available
    components: return_period_p90, max_frac_reaches, length_days, rain_max_24h_mm.

Inputs : data/zcta (steps 9-10), data/final (step 7), data/rain (12), data/coastal (13)
Outputs: data/final_zcta/
Usage  : python 14_final_event_zcta_table.py
"""

